secubox-ytsas (0.1.3-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * FIX conserved MP3/FLAC (and other common audio) went to PeerTube — a video
    platform — because secubox-ytsas-conserve uploaded every conserved file
    through peertubectl regardless of type. It now classifies each file
    (extension-based; ambiguous .mkv is content-probed via ffprobe when
    available) and routes audio to Lyrion (`lyrionctl ingest`) while video
    keeps going to PeerTube unchanged. Destination per category is declarative
    — [conserve] video/audio in ytsas.toml — not hardcoded. An unrecognised
    file type is never routed anywhere (terminal error, dequeued); an absent
    or unreachable Lyrion leaves the item queued for a later retry, exactly
    like the existing "peertubectl not installed" degrade path (ref #967).
  * Recommends: secubox-lyrion, ffmpeg (ffprobe resolves ambiguous containers).
  * library.py/main.py: a conserved-to-Lyrion item now records into its own
    lyrion_status/lyrion_path columns instead of falling through into
    peertube_status='done' with no url — the previous shape made a
    successful Lyrion conserve look neither done nor failed in the panel,
    inviting a redundant re-click. www/ytsas/index.html shows a distinct
    "🎵 Lyrion ✓" badge alongside "📼 PeerTube ✓".
  * lyrionctl ingest: namespace the destination by a hash of the source path
    (not just its basename) — two unrelated conserved files that happen to
    share a filename no longer silently overwrite each other in the library.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200

